// Cloudflare Workers config for pitch-sim.com.
//
// Serves the Vite build (Phase 2). Cloudflare Workers Builds is connected to
// the GitHub repo and runs `npm ci && npm run build:app` to produce dist/,
// then `npx wrangler deploy` — so this directory must match Vite's outDir in
// vite.config.ts. Non-production branches get `wrangler versions upload`
// instead, which is the phone-testable preview URL.
//
// Note: .assetsignore is read from the assets directory, so the one at the
// repo root no longer applies. It doesn't need to: dist/ contains only build
// output, so src/, docs/ and repo tooling can't leak into the served site.
//
// `main` + `assets.binding` (ROADMAP.md item 7): the presence of `main`
// switches this from an assets-only Worker to "Workers with assets" — the
// entry script now sees every request first and must explicitly fall through
// to `env.ASSETS.fetch(request)` for anything it doesn't own (functions/
// _worker.js does this). PocketRPG's file-based `functions/api/**` routing
// is a Cloudflare *Pages* mechanism and doesn't apply to a plain Worker
// deploy like this one — functions/_worker.js is a small manual router
// instead, kept in the same file layout for portability.
//
// `d1_databases`: `database_id` below is a PLACEHOLDER. It has not been
// created yet — this session has no Cloudflare account access (`wrangler
// whoami` → not authenticated). Before this can deploy for real:
//   1. `wrangler d1 create pitch-db` and paste the real database_id here.
//   2. `wrangler d1 migrations apply pitch-db --remote` to run migrations/.
//   3. Register a Google OAuth client (console.cloud.google.com) with
//      authorized redirect URIs for both the workers.dev URL and (once the
//      domain cutover lands) pitch-sim.com's own /api/auth/google/callback.
//   4. `wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`,
//      `JWT_SECRET` (a long random string — `openssl rand -hex 32`).
// `wrangler dev` works today without any of the above: it runs main against
// a local SQLite D1 (`wrangler d1 migrations apply pitch-db --local`), and
// the auth routes degrade to a clean 500 "not configured" without secrets.
{
	"name": "pitch",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-08-24",
	"main": "functions/_worker.js",
	"assets": {
		"directory": "./dist",
		"binding": "ASSETS",
		"not_found_handling": "404-page"
	},
	"d1_databases": [
		{
			"binding": "DB",
			"database_name": "pitch-db",
			"database_id": "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_D1_DATABASE_ID"
		}
	],
	"observability": {
		"enabled": true
	}
}
